 "content": "# Continual-ARC task 3a6ed935

Observed rule from demo + correct test: Given a lone 1 and 2 on a blank grid, connect them with a one-cell-wide trail of 3s. Move diagonally from the 1 toward the 2 as far as possible while keeping one step short of the target in the shorter coordinate direction; then move straight along the remaining (longer-difference) coordinate until the final 3 is diagonally adjacent to the 2. Leave both endpoint cells unchanged. Equivalently, trace a diagonal staircase segment followed by an orthogonal straight segment, ending at the cell one row and one column away from the 2.

Evidence: Demo 1 at (row 10,col 1), 2 at (row 3,col 11): 3s go diagonally up-right to (4,7), then right to (4,10), diagonally adjacent to 2. Test at (1,4) and (13,12): 3s go diagonally down-right through (8,11), then down through (12,11), diagonally adjacent to 2. Coordinates here are 1-based. Preserve all other 0s."
